Getting a inspired from your YANI, and having way too much free time
today, here are some YANIs or YAOIs (I vaguely remember at least one
Magic Memory Vault/Ludios YANI thread but I'm too lazy to go look for
it; probably many of these are derivative):

* The walls and stone around a broken-into memory vault will sometimes
be repaired like a shop's walls. (Same messages). Living things are
booted out at this time. Corridor squares in some radius around the
shop will also be turned to stone.

* Some percentage (50%?) of leprechauns are in the employ of Croesus.
When one of these leprechauns teleports successfully, it automatically
deposits all carried gold in a MMV if the level has one and it is
intact. If no good MMV, maybe it goes to the MMV account  (see below),
maybe not.

* If there is an empty, intact vault on the level then sometimes an
invisible, awake, hostile leprechaun in the service of Croesus will be
generated. Or a small team of them.

* Earth elementals will sometimes "un-dig" and turn corridors into
stone making them the anti rock mole. Oops, wrong list.

* Sometimes a guard will whisk away the gold in a vault. When this
happens, the amount is added to the "MMV account". When a new vault is
made on level creation, some gold may be added from this account (in
addition to what's there).

* Guards/invisible demons will whisk away the money in an MMV when a)
there's gold in the vault but it has been breached, b) when the player
is in the vault but the guard doesn't like the answer (small % chance,
or based on parsing the answer "That's not a name!"), c) the hero in
the vault is a greedy or metallivorous monster ("You don't look
trustworthy!" -- should always happen to dwarves and rogues), d) any
greedy/metallivorous monster is in the vault.

* Sometimes you really do hear searching: a room is randomly checked.
All loose gold in the room is swept into the nearest MMV (or added to
the account if the MMV is not intact? -- or happens on all levels not
just MMV ones?). If the player can see one of these locations a guard
appears there or nearby briefly ("I'll take this." "Don't mind me." "I
believe this belongs to Croesus"). Could be amusing for careless
players buying protection.

* If the player's max depth is low enough, and the ludios portal has
not been created, and the MMV vault on the current level is intact and
has gold, there is a small chance that the ludios portal will be
created.

* When entering a level that hasn't been visited in awhile, sometimes
repair its vault and fill it with gold from the account.

* When a player pays a priest or shopkeeper, 10% of the payment is
lost and added to the MMV account. When a player drops gold on the
floor of a shop, 10% of the gold is removed (the player still receives
100% credit). Make devil bribes pay 10% too, for what it's worth --
even devils have to make deals with Croesus.

* Few if any of all special MMV things happen if Croesus is dead.

* If Croesus is dead and an old level is loaded, all gold is removed
from the MMV (greedy guards).

* Make Croesus a leprechaun instead of a human for no reason in
particular.

